# UnrealMCP5_6_1 Project Binding

## Project Facts

- Repository: `UnrealMCP5_6_1`; embedded operating root: `./codex`; integration/default branch: `main`. Paths in this file are relative to the discovered repository root.
- Cubeless fork: `origin` -> `https://github.com/cubeless2-lgtm/UnrealMCP5_6_1.git`; optional original `upstream` -> `https://github.com/chongdashu/unreal-mcp.git` (fetch-only for routine work). These identify expected remotes, not permission to rewrite local configuration.
- Project: `MCPGameProject/MCPGameProject.uproject`, `EngineAssociation` `5.6`; editor build target: `MCPGameProjectEditor Win64 Development`.
- Operating routes are in `codex/AGENTS.md`; component details are conditional through `codex/docs/workflows/component-reading-router.md`. Android packaging requires explicit task scope.
- Project-system/study/review index: `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/README.md`; read only the system relevant to the task.
- Historical sources: `codex/snapshots/UnrealMCP5_6_1-instructions-before-consolidation-20260824.md` and `codex/snapshots/20260906-before-bootstrap-dedup/project-binding.md`. They are immutable evidence, not active instructions.

## Engine And Bridge

- Target UE 5.6.1 under the root adapter's absolute capability boundary. No machine-wide default engine path is prescribed; resolve the effective installation with `codex/docs/policies/workspace-portability.md`, including its engine resolution rules.
- For donor code, reimplement only UE 5.6-compatible behavior in the existing architecture. Confirm APIs in the resolved engine's UE 5.6 headers or by its build before promotion; omit capabilities that cannot be demonstrated.
- Preserve compatibility guards and stable response keys. For unavailable UE 5.7-only data, retain the fallback field with an `unavailable_in_ue_5_6` note.
- Resolve the effective configured bridge endpoint at runtime. Default: `127.0.0.1:55561`; `UNREAL_MCP_5_6_1_PORT` or `-UnrealMCPPort=` may override it. Do not substitute a UE 5.7 default or generic `UNREAL_MCP_PORT`.
- Port defaults are not proof of editor/project identity. Check the connected editor's project and effective endpoint before bridge work; coordinate shared-editor lifecycle using the common instructions.

## Maintenance Constraints

- Keep Cubeless patches narrow and reviewable; do not broadly rewrite upstream files.
- The approved split under `MCPGameProject/Plugins/UnrealMCP/Source/UnrealMCP/Private/Commands/` permits only behavior-preserving separation with unchanged classes and routing.
- Upstream workflow: `codex/docs/workflows/mcp-upstream-update.md`; preferred helper: `scripts/update_with_pcg_extension.ps1`. Preserve the generic Python bridge, PCG/AI texture layers, and UE 5.6.1 guards; load domain documents only for affected components.

## Verification Entry Point

- Dispatcher: `Python/scripts/analysis/run_verification.py`. Execute commands below from the discovered repository root.
- Implementation, executable workflow/configuration, or shared-contract promotion requires a complete passing result of the offline profile below. Promotion and valid evidence reuse are defined in `codex/docs/policies/cost-control.md`; when an equivalent result is not already established, run:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\analysis\run_verification.py --profile full
```

- Cadence, documentation-only Tier 0, independent review, and evidence reuse remain defined in `codex/docs/policies/cost-control.md`. Focused development selects an explicit profile: `core`, `catalog`, `transport`, `schema`, `niagara`, `write-observer`, `release-offline`, or `windows-transport`. Focused passes do not replace required `full`; no automatic changed-file/path skipping is enabled.
- When bridge/tool integration changes and a compatible editor is available, run the read-only live smoke:

```powershell
uv --directory .\Python run python scripts\smoke_live_bridge.py
```

- Exit code 2 is no reachable editor: report a skip, never a pass.
- For UnrealMCP C++ or build-metadata changes, build the editor target above against the resolved UE 5.6 engine and this project's `.uproject`. Run affected live/build checks through the matching workflow; avoid full source-engine rebuilds unless necessary or explicitly requested.
- GitHub Actions use the same dispatcher: Ubuntu `full`, Windows transport `windows-transport`.
